6. A Simple Comparison Checklist

Use this checklist when researching two or three programmes:

Confirm the degree and awarding institution.

Request the complete fee breakdown.

Check the UPSC preparation structure.

Compare class timings and academic workload.

Review study resources and assessment support.

Understand payment and refund conditions.

Calculate accommodation and living costs, if applicable.

Discuss the overall commitment with your family.

Conclusion

Choosing a degree alongside UPSC coaching is an important decision that combines education planning, preparation goals, and financial responsibility. Comparing complete costs and programme structures can help students make a more informed choice.

The most suitable programme is one that fits the student's academic needs, budget, and ability to maintain a sustainable study routine.

